      "factionId": "dawn_guard",
      "startingWeaponIds": ["training_sword"],
      "startingItemIds": ["field_tonic"],
      "experiencePerLevel": 50,
      "growthRates": {
        "health": 90,
        "strength": 55,
        "defense": 45,
        "resistance": 20,
        "movement": 10,
        "actionPoints": 5
      },
      "notes": "A rider who survives the crossing has felled a picket, which is sixty experience against fifty a level, so the muster road is one level long. None of the six chances is a hundred, so every one of them is rolled: what the level gives is what the growth stream said, not what the author hoped."
    },
    {
      "id": "river_watch_unit",
      "name": "River Watch",
      "classId": "guard",
      "factionId": "river_watch",
      "startingWeaponIds": ["training_sword"],
      "experienceAward": 60,
      "dropItemId": "field_tonic",
      "dropChance": 60,
      "notes": "A picket leaves its tonic three times in five. Sixty rather than a hundred on purpose: a certainty rolls nothing at all, and the point of the muster road is that the drop stream is really drawn from. What falls goes to the campaign's store when the battle ends, not into the rider's pack mid-fight."
    }
  ],
